Reason: every destroy rewrites stale copies of the dead instance's id, and patches 0025 and 0061 already limit that to
instances flagged as holding id-like numbers and to their listed variables, but finding those instances still walked
all of runner->instances, reading each one's flags: about one cache miss per instance. In the mine room (rm_a5c22) a
chain of Robo Mines keeps 1,100 to 1,800 instances alive and destroys a dozen or more a frame, so on the real Wii each
destroy cost ~230 µs and the rewrites 1.3 to 4.8 ms a frame. The instances in runner->instances that were given an
id-like number are now kept in a list (an instance knows whether it is in runner->instances and its place in the
list, both kept where it joins or leaves the room's list or is freed), and a high id's rewrite walks only that list,
with the same per-instance tests and the same per-instance work, so the same slots are rewritten (~5 µs a destroy).
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

